  "title": "Kodera2023: Left/right-hand motor-imagery EEG dataset",
  "description": "A left/right-hand motor-imagery EEG dataset from 29 healthy participants recorded at the University of West Bohemia for brain-computer interface research. Participants performed cue-based, single-class imagery of left- or right-hand movement across four runs in one session. The data are re-released in BIDS format with HED event annotations via MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with BrainVision Recorder (BrainProducts) using the standard 10-20 montage. The README gives 9 channels (Fz, Cz, Pz, F3, F4, P3, P4, C3, C4) sampled at 500 Hz, while its description mentions two cohorts (16-channel 500 Hz and 9-channel 1000 Hz). Each recording is one imagery class, with 4 s trials and the cue onset marked by a stimulus marker. Line frequency was 50 Hz.",
